# C, the coupling matrix: an observed dependence between two layers' remainders. One row per
# (filing, from_layer, to_layer), which is the sparse form of an L x L matrix.
#
# Every row contradicts the assumption
#   C = 0 is this model's assumption, so every row here is somebody contradicting it with an
#   observation. That is why the observation is required rather than optional: a coupling is never
#   derived, never inferred from correlation, and never filed as a number alone. Somebody watched
#   two layers move together and wrote down what they saw.
#
# No rows says nothing by itself
#   A filing with no couplings has either a stack of independent layers or nobody who looked, and
#   those are opposite claims. Which one it is lives in `coupling_search` (see
#   epistemics/searches.sqlc) and not in this relation. Densify this into a grid of 0.0 and the
#   difference is gone for good.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings/pm:coupling, each carrying its pm:observed.
SELECT c.filing, c.from_layer, c.to_layer,
       c.low, c.mode, c.high, c.unit, c.strength_absent, c.observation
FROM pm.coupling c
